# Hackathon rules (binding)

Source of truth: `docs/context/hackathon-rules.md`. Do not invent extra organizer policy.

**Task:** small **open-weights** model on the **Polish history (historia) matura**. Venue Kolektyw3, 25–27 Sep 2026.

## Hard constraints

- Each model as run on the exam: **≤ 8 GB on disk**. Quantized OK. Several models OK, each ≤ 8 GB. **LoRA adapters and RAG knowledge bases do not count.**
- **Exam is offline:** no ChatGPT/Claude/Gemini or other closed APIs, **no web search**. Local RAG + tools OK.
- Closed LLM APIs **are allowed while building** (e.g. synthetic data).
- **Training ends Sun 11:00**; exam is provided then. Exam script uses `TEAM_KEY` and sends **answers only**.
- Submit **base model** and **trained model** results (progress track). With several models, baseline = highest-scoring model **alone**.
- Own pre-hackathon fine-tunes **cannot** be declared as the bare base (disqualification). Public already-tuned history models are OK; that score is the benchmark.
- Graded work starts Fri 18:00. Repo for jury **before Sun 11:00**. Roster **Sat 12:00**.
- Inference must be fast: **a few minutes** for the full exam **and** presentation on stage.

## Repo and prizes

- No copyrighted scans/unlicensed datasets in git. List sources + a **fetch/process script**. No paywall/login/ToS bypass.
- Wikipedia / derived data: **CC BY-SA-compatible**. Model licence follows the HF card.
- `SOURCE.md` must contain exactly: `Made during the Warsaw Model Trainers hackathon, Kolektyw3, 25–27.09.2026` (required for any prize).
- Prize tracks: best matura score · best progress vs base · smallest model with **≥ 35%** ("Mały, ale wariat").
- Harness-only (RAG, prompts, agents, tools) can compete. System prompts / few-shot / CoT count as harness.

Submission format: announced Saturday — do not guess a format.
